# s9_encrypt_chunk_inplace: chunked encryption assembles its result in place (no two copies of the
# embedding share during concatenation). Free.
#
# object     p_graphop_s8 (per-node VmHWM markers on s8): high-water changes three times in the run:
#              776,248 kB   already at the first graph node (embeddings.Shape)
#              835,588 kB   +59,340  after layer.intermediate.intermediate_act_fn.GELU
#              845,332 kB    +9,744  after the same GELU in another layer
#            91.8% of the peak before any graph node; poller: 1,410 ms after embed|after_convert,
#            293 ms before embed|after_encrypt (inside enc_embed.encrypt()). s8 reduced that transient:
#              before s8   601,612 kB
#              after  s8   384,348 kB      -36% (donor comment: ~-88%)
# remainder  crypten.cat(enc_chunks, dim=0) holds eight inputs and the output: 2 x 173,976 kB
#            (28,996 x 768 x 8 B) = 347,952 vs 384,348 measured.
# lever      output share allocated at the first chunk; each later chunk copied into its row range, then
#            freed. Live: 173,976 + 21,747 = 195,723 kB.
# free       same eight encryptions, order and generator; same bytes and row order.
# gate       identical to s8's expected. Lever refuses on a row-count mismatch (torch.chunk may return
#            fewer chunks; misordered rows give plausible logits).
# expected   -~188,000 kB, peak 660,000 to 700,000 vs 881,272 (-20% to -25%). Below 660,000: GELU binding
#            (p_graphop_s8: +69,084 kB, the only graph op raising the high-water).
SHAFT_SCRIPT=$BASE/bert_perlayer_stream_cpu.py
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_chunk_inplace_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu,embed_chunk_cpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16 SHAFT_ENC_CHUNKS=8"
